        <item>
            <title>The Ebenezer Scrooge model: Can Yom Kippur really bring repentance and change?</title>
            <link>https://www.jpost.com/judaism/jewish-holidays/article-908556</link>
            <description>&lt;img align="right" alt="YOM KIPPUR asks us to confront who we were, who we have become, and who we might yet become. (photo credit: MARC ISRAEL SELLEM/THE JERUSALEM POST)" src="https://images.jpost.com/image/upload/f_auto,fl_lossy/q_auto/c_fill,g_faces:center,h_1312,w_1969/738422" title="YOM KIPPUR asks us to confront who we were, who we have become, and who we might yet become. (photo credit: MARC ISRAEL SELLEM/THE JERUSALEM POST)" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;From Dickens’s Ebenezer Scrooge to modern psychology, the journey from remorse to lasting behavioral change reveals why Yom Kippur can be both a reckoning and a starting point.&lt;br /&gt;</description>
            <pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 23:44:01 GMT</pubDate>
        </item>
        <item>
            <title>Israel tore itself apart on Yom Kippur - then October 7 reminded us of our collective 'we'</title>
            <link>https://www.jpost.com/judaism/jewish-holidays/article-908554</link>
            <description>&lt;img align="right" alt="The Orthodox Jewish group of Rosh Yehudi sets up a gender partition during a public prayer for Yom Kippur, on Dizengoff Square, Tel Aviv, September 24, 2023 (photo credit: TOMER NEUBERG/FLASH90)" src="https://images.jpost.com/image/upload/f_auto,fl_lossy/q_auto/c_fill,g_faces:center,h_5504,w_8256/737722" title="The Orthodox Jewish group of Rosh Yehudi sets up a gender partition during a public prayer for Yom Kippur, on Dizengoff Square, Tel Aviv, September 24, 2023 (photo credit: TOMER NEUBERG/FLASH90)" /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;On Yom Kippur of 2023, Jews were pitted against Jews across the country. Thirteen days later, October 7 would remind Israelis that beneath their deepest divisions, there was still a collective “we.”&lt;br /&gt;</description>
            <pubDate>Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:52:35 GMT</pubDate>
        </item>
